    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_8762129c59cbb812b3de14c21d17eac05b35f5d378856c7916a9377ece09b6dd",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: the visible proof splits at a threshold set for f(t), uses Holder-type comparisons between even and higher moments, chooses parameters, treats the opposite sign analogously, and ends by translating a positive-proportion count discrepancy into an interval containing no zero of the other L-function. Interpretation: threshold measure is the bridge from earlier moment estimates to zero-gap geometry; Holder and thresholding do not create the positive-measure conclusion without those prior estimates. Boundary: f and the consumed moment estimates are outside this unit, and OCR prevents quantitative certification of powers, constants, and parameter choices.",
